{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "template_id": "claude-binder-lane.v1",
  "base_profile": "small-run.template.json",
  "gap_notes": {
    "read_me": "This profile is the small run on user-owned Modal compute. It inherits every scientific choice from small-run.template.json and replaces only the four provider-facing adapter bindings. A value written __REQUIRED__ comes from the operator's own Claude Science session. compose accepts those placeholders and materialize refuses them, so a run cannot start on an unread value. references/modal-bring-up.md lists the calls that produce each one.",
    "backbone_generator": "The Modal route generates with RFdiffusion, not RFdiffusion3. rfdiffusion3_generator.py reaches its model over an HTTPS deployment and requires --fal-url, so it has no Modal binding. This profile restores the RFdiffusion command that full-ensemble.template.json declares, which is the binding every other Modal profile in this package uses. --contigs stays __REQUIRED__ because the contig string describes one target and one binder length window.",
    "control_builder": "control_builder.py runs the rescore arm as a child process rather than as its own stage, so the arm inherits whatever container the builder is in. The builder therefore carries the same esmfold2_gpu binding as the predictor. Without it the control panel would fold on the session kernel, which has neither CUDA nor MPS.",
    "timing_basis": "A guarded Modal campaign completed all 16 stages and recorded 622 seconds of provider-job wall time, but its 4.2837978 USD figure is an admission-control estimate and not a settled per-stage bill. That integrated run is not a portable per-candidate rate for another target or account. Keep this profile's timing fields operator-resolved, beginning with a single-candidate canary as described in references/modal-bring-up.md section 4.",
    "predictor_arms": "One ESMFold2 mode runs here, the same as the inherited profile. A guarded Modal campaign exercised ESMFold2-Fast. The esmfold2_gpu environment also carries the full checkpoint, but this profile deliberately omits that different-MSA arm; qualifying Fast does not establish Full for a new target.",
    "generator_identity": "This profile substitutes RFdiffusion for the RFdiffusion3 its base runs. The base reaches RFdiffusion3 over an HTTPS deployment, which no container route provides, so the generator here is RFdiffusion and the tool id says so. The adapter id stays rfdiffusion-generator because that names the backbone generator slot, not the tool filling it."
  },
